+### 7. Orphans
+Publish never deletes (`publish.luau`), so a raft made by `new raft` over prepared issues and then released stays on `origin/main` at `new` with no member. Nothing reads its `issues:` (§1), so it holds nothing. `audit` warns (never an error, so `main` stays green): `orphan-raft <path>: <R> is a given-back raft with no member: retire it with ./zn recombine <a raft of its project and type> <R>`, for a backlog raft whose status is `new`/`new-…` and that no issue's `raft:` names. `recombine <K> <orphan>` moves nothing and retires the orphan in the rafting PR (retirement lands by PR). On today's tree the warning already finds one: R0040 (`status: new-…`, `issues: []`).
+
+**A retired raft keeps its history** (review 001 F2). R0040 holds five design reviews, five refutes and a `harvest.md`; deleting its folder would make `lessons --check` fail (a lesson loses its only source) and drop five rounds from metrics. So `recombine` moves a retired raft's whole folder to `<root>/rafts/retired/<R-id>` and sets `retired: <keeper>` in its document. The readers:
+- the walkers checked against the full gate on a copy holding a retired raft (E3; review 002 F2): `store`, the board's collection, `sweepStale`, `migrate`, `paths`, `trail` and `history` read only the lifecycle folders, which is intended (history counts issues only, and trail has no capture for rafts); `audit`, `lessons`, `metrics`, `compact` and `tests/lib/engine.luau`'s `engine.empty` read or clear `retired/`; and the promoted c0114/classified and c0043/rounds are overridden to read it too;
+- the item finders (`store.find`, `store.all`, the board's collection, `raft-plan`, `ready`, `status`) read only the backlog, `active/` and `done/` folders, so a retired raft is never found, drawn or worked (`retired` is not an id, so the backlog scan skips the folder);
+- `lessons.load` reads `retired/` too (`{"", "/active", "/done", "/retired"}`), so its reviews and harvest stay lesson sources;
+- `metrics` (`retiredRafts()`) keeps its rows in "Review rounds per raft" and "Design-review cost per round" (its spend went with its members, so its minutes are 0) and in the before/after split, dated by its `created:`;
+- `audit` scans `retired/` as raft folders (their ids stay in use, their documents are checked), never warns about them as orphans, and reports `retired-raft` for an issue there or a raft document without `retired:` (only `recombine` makes one);
+- `compact` renumbers them with the rest (it renumbers what `audit.scan` finds);
+- `metrics` lists them in id order with the other rafts (c0043 pins one sorted list).
+Proved on a copy of today's tree (E2): `recombine R0030 R0040` leaves `lessons --check` ok (21 lessons, 118 harvest entries) and metrics' `| R0040 | 5 | 0 | second-order |`.
