+- **U1. Does the `raft:` line conflict in every merge path?** Run 2026-10-21 in the scratchpad (`c0116-work/u1.sh`, a throwaway repository, never this one): two branches set `raft:` to R0050 and R0051 from one base, the first squash-merged into `main`. (a) `git merge main` on the second: `CONFLICT`. (b) `git merge --squash` of the second onto `main` (GitHub's squash merge): `CONFLICT`. (c) a third branch with the identical edit (`raft: R0050`): merges cleanly (harmless: the same raft). (d) a branch that only edits the adjacent `depends_on:`: `CONFLICT` (the false alarm F10 names, in the safe direction). (e) a rebase of the second onto `main`: `CONFLICT (content)`. **PASS.** The claims spec repeats (a) through the real commands.
+- **U2. Do the stamp-keyed rules keep the promoted specs green?** Run on the prototype: the full gate (Verification log), with c0053's four command specs, c0067, c0068, c0070/board-refresh and c0081/remap named again in AC9. **PASS**, after the overrides below (all five are text or count pins of what c0116 deliberately changes) and one code fix the gate found (c0081's publish guard: `refuseStale()` must sit right before each new `publish.commit`).
+- **U3. Can size be estimated before code?** Run 2026-10-21 on the prototype's done issues with a `spend.md` and promoted specs (12 had both): predicted changed lines = k × acceptance-spec lines + m × Touched paths, fitted on half. Best fit: 50% of the training half within ±50%, **17%** of the test half. **FAIL**: no cheap formula. Fallback taken: the designer writes `size:` (z-design §3), and `metrics` reports estimate against actual (the size table) so the estimates can be calibrated afterwards. Guess G4.
+- **U4. Is the no-argument plan deterministic and judgement-free?** Every rule in §3 is a pure function of the records; the plan spec shuffles a nine-issue, three-raft backlog 20 times and gets one plan; `./zn raft-plan` on the prototype's real backlog prints "nothing to raft" (every prepared issue has a raft today). **PASS.** The only model steps are the raft's prose and the coherence review (z-raft §3, §4), which c0117 runs attended or as model steps.
+- **U5. Where do design reviews live, and does anything promoted read them under a raft?** `grep -rl design-review` over the engine and `tests/acceptance`: the readers are `lessons.luau` (every item folder already), `metrics` (raft folders only: changed), `trail.luau` and `ledger.luau` (names only). Promoted specs pinning the raft-only count: c0043/rounds (overridden). **PASS.**
+- **U6. Raft-level coherence for grouped features**: the user decided "Short coherence review" (Problem).
+- **E2. A retired raft keeps what its readers count** (review 001 F2). Run 2026-10-21 on a copy of today's tree (a scratch clone with its own bare origin, in the scratchpad, never this repository): before, `./zn lessons --check` said "21 lessons, 118 harvest entries, ok" and `metrics` listed `| R0040 | 5 | 0 | second-order |`; `./zn recombine R0030 R0040` moved R0040's folder to `z-nile/.tracker/rafts/retired/R0040` with `retired: R0030`; after, `lessons --check` said the same, metrics kept `| R0040 | 5 | 0 | second-order |`, `audit` had no orphan warning, and the carried `status R0030 prepared` succeeded with no new review. **PASS.** The first draft's `git rm -r` turned `lessons --check` red (the reviewer's run).
+- **E3. The full gate on a copy of today's tree with a raft retired** (review 002 F2; lesson testing/prove-state-folders-on-the-real-tree). Run 2026-10-21 in a scratch clone (in the scratchpad, with its own bare origin; its identity was set to a non-fixture one, because the tripwire refuses a checkout whose identity looks like a fixture's): `recombine R0030 R0040`, the carried `status R0030 prepared`, a commit, then `z-nile/check.sh --full`. Before the fixes: 1049 passed, 3 failed: c0005/worktree (`engine.empty` left the retired folder), c0043/rounds ("lists every raft once") and c0114/classified ("raft skill-lessons: not found"), exactly the reviewer's three. After them, retired.spec runs c0114/classified and c0043/rounds on a clone holding a retired raft, and they pass; `engine.empty` clears `retired/` (M77). **PASS.**
+- **E1. Mutation check.** 88 mutants (M1 to M91 without M11, M12 and M60, whose guard round 3 removed as subsumed), each applied alone to the prototype in a scratch worktree (`.worktree/mut-c0116-{1,2,3}`, detached, removed after) by the scratchpad runner (`c0116-work/mutrun.sh`, `mutants.py`), its spec run, then reverted. Round 4 added M89 to M91 (review 004 F1 and F2) and reran the mutants the round's code touched; the final count is under Verification log. Round 2 added M69 to M78 (review 002 F1 to F4), and all were killed on the first run. Round 1 (round 1 added M57 to M68 for review 001 F1, F2, F3, F5 and F7; M66 first raised a Lua error instead of failing an assertion, so it was rewritten as "a sizeless member counts 0", the draft's rule, and killed; M64 first survived because the retired R0150 carries recombine's `preparing-` stamp, so no orphan warning could fire, and the case gained a retired raft whose document still says `new` (lesson testing/guard-needs-its-own-case)). Four needed a stronger case first: M24 (recombine's raft-level type check) survived because the members' own type check also refused, so the case gained an empty feature raft (an orphan of another type, where only the raft check can refuse); M27 (recombine's membership check) survived because the publish's origin check refuses the same input with another message, so the case now pins `c0031 is not a member of R0020`, the message §2 states; M4 and M21 first failed on a spec-side file read (a missing claim file, a deleted folder), and their cases now assert the file or folder before reading it. M54 to M56 were added after the first run, when the table showed `fold`'s own project, type and backlog refusals had no case.
