+# Review 003: c0116 (design mode)
+Inputs: prep-c0116 at 715097b (`c0116.md`, `check.sh`, `acceptance/*`, `design-review-00{1,2}.md`, `design-refute-00{1,2}.md`, `harvest.md`); prototype `.worktree/proto-c0116` at 7543c85 (on `proto-c0115` 0b9aae2), the record code read (`raftplan.designHash`/`parseGrouped`, `recordGrouped`, `regrouped`, the carried move, `ready`, `unfold`, `recombine`), `z-raft` §4–§5, `compact.apply`; `./zn capture c0116` (fb7fd80: Problem and Solution unchanged, prep additions marked); `./zn lessons --when design --full`. Every run was in scratch clones of the prototype with the origin remote removed (`scratchpad/c0116-review003/clone{,2}`), fixtures under their own `.cache`. Reproductions: `scratchpad/c0116-review003/rv3.spec.luau`.
+Dropped from review-002: F1 (round 2's `rv2.spec.luau` rerun unchanged: S1's `ready` now says "c0020 (348b94e3a860 → 7033c9cca191) changed on origin/main since R0010 grouped it", S5's carried move refuses c0040 the same way), F2 (`clone2`: R0040 retired as `recombine` does it, committed; `z-nile/check.sh --full` **GATE PASSED** with 1068 + 1053 cases, no c0115 patch needed; `./zn check c0116` 9/9; `audit` 0 errors; `lessons --check` ok, 27 lessons, 130 harvest entries), F3 (`unfold` works on a landed raft, and z-design's claim succeeds after it), F4 (the refusal now names the recovery).
+
+Held this round (no finding): `stop` then `ready` again on a grouped raft (no false refusal: ready and stop change only `status:` and folder paths, which the hash leaves out); a forged hash in `grouped:` (refused, naming both values); `unfold` against another terminal's open rafting (refused: R is `preparing` with a stamp it doesn't remember) and against `ready` (both are lease publishes on R's status line); `recombine` re-hashing the members it moves (a redesign caught in O is re-recorded in K, but K's membership changed, so K needs a coherence review written in this branch, which reads the new design). Guesses: G15, G17, G18 are reasonable; G16 is reasonable as the choice of recording over restamping, but its "the engine checks only the record" is F2; G19 is the user's call, and F1–F4's fixes add perhaps 60–100 lines to its 1,670.
+
+### F1 [high] The record hashes only the issue's document: a redesign of its `check.sh` or acceptance specs inside the rafting window passes the carried move and `ready`
+Where: §1 "What was grouped is recorded" ("a hash of each prepared member's document"); §2 `raftplan.designHash(text)`; `recordGrouped` (`git show origin/main:<doc>`); G16.
+Evidence: reproduced (`rv3.spec.luau` T1). A runs `new raft chore chk c0010 c0020`, writes Theme, Order and `design-review-001.md`. B runs `status c0020 preparing`, adds `check "AC2: NEW CRITERION"` to c0020's `check.sh` and a new `acceptance/new.spec.luau`, runs `status c0020 prepared` and lands. A syncs; the carried `status R0010 prepared` **succeeds**; A lands; `./zn ready R0010` **succeeds** ("readied R0010 … (c0010, c0020)"), and the readied `active/c0020/check.sh` holds the new criterion that no coherence review read.
+Critique: third round on the "a redesign inside the window" mechanism. The record is the right shape; its coverage is not. An issue's design is its document plus its sequestered contract (`check.sh`, `acceptance/**`), and z-design's own cycle also writes design-review, refute and harvest files in the issue folder (§6). The tempting fix (hash `check.sh` too) leaves the acceptance specs and the issue's own review files out.
