+Candidate lesson (for the lead, a note on architecture/one-reader-per-format): "git's view" is two views, the index and the working tree as `git add -A` would see it. Choose one per reader for what that reader's commit will carry, and make every rewrite that hashes before and after start from a clean tree. Check: "Can a file that this command will not commit change a hash it compares?"
